S-4, the registry: searches after the clerk has entered all four, and first, before it does anything else with the entry and before any write (against S-3, gap 7); it looks among learners only; it compares the family name, the given names and the date of birth; two values that differ in capitals only are the same, and every difference but capitals makes two values differ; it does not compare the school, which is entered and saved and never searched on, nor any field but the three; it does not read the key table. If it finds exactly one learner the goal goes on at S-5; if it finds none, at S-6; on more than one, at F-4.
